      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Eventually, the lights come up and the rectangular screen goes black. The humans stand up and leave the room, chatting and laughing, and showing signs of pleasure.",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        109,
        1124,
        165
      ],
      "block_id": 1,
      "block_order": 2,
      "group_id": 1,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          67.0,
          109.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          109.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          165.0
        ],
        [
          67.0,
          165.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Why do these humans voluntarily expose themselves to what appears to be a deeply unpleasant experience? And why do they react so strongly to those patterns of light on a screen?",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        170,
        1124,
        227
      ],
      "block_id": 2,
      "block_order": 3,
      "group_id": 2,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          67.0,
          170.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          170.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          227.0
        ],
        [
          67.0,
          227.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "I am fascinated with the paradox of horror --- the strange fact that many people seek out scary entertainment.",
      "block_bbox": [
        109,
        233,
        1032,
        259
      ],
      "block_id": 3,
      "block_order": 4,
      "group_id": 3,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          109.0,
          233.0
        ],
        [
          1032.0,
          233.0
        ],
        [
          1032.0,
          259.0
        ],
        [
          109.0,
          259.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "I think the answer to the puzzle lies in human nature.",
      "block_bbox": [
        108,
        264,
        562,
        289
      ],
      "block_id": 4,
      "block_order": 5,
      "group_id": 4,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          108.0,
          264.0
        ],
        [
          562.0,
          264.0
        ],
        [
          562.0,
          289.0
        ],
        [
          108.0,
          289.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "My research suggests that we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations that allow us to experience negative emotions in a safe context. You can see these elements of horror in children's games. Take hide-and-seek for example, which is a simulation of a predator-prey interaction. The kid hides and the adult pretends to be a predator, searching for the child while howling like a dangerous beast.",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        296,
        1124,
        414
      ],
      "block_id": 5,
      "block_order": 6,
      "group_id": 5,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          296.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          296.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          414.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          414.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "This simulation gives the child crucial information about how to avoid becoming prey, and children tend to find that kind of activity deeply satisfying, presumably because it gives them a safe experience of a potentially catastrophic scenario.",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        420,
        1122,
        476
      ],
      "block_id": 6,
      "block_order": 7,
      "group_id": 6,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          67.0,
          420.0
        ],
        [
          1122.0,
          420.0
        ],
        [
          1122.0,
          476.0
        ],
        [
          67.0,
          476.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "They find it pleasurable, and pleasure is evolution's way of motivating us toward adaptive behaviour.",
      "block_bbox": [
        108,
        482,
        971,
        508
      ],
      "block_id": 7,
      "block_order": 8,
      "group_id": 7,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          108.0,
          482.0
        ],
        [
          971.0,
          482.0
        ],
        [
          971.0,
          508.0
        ],
        [
          108.0,
          508.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Horror is pleasurable to many people because it lets us play with negative emotions and develop coping strategies. We learn what it feels like to be truly afraid, and we learn how to handle negative emotion.",
      "block_bbox": [
        72,
        514,
        1122,
        570
      ],
      "block_id": 8,
      "block_order": 9,
      "group_id": 8,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          72.0,
          514.0
        ],
        [
          1122.0,
          514.0
        ],
        [
          1122.0,
          570.0
        ],
        [
          72.0,
          570.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "How, then, does horror work? My research suggests that horror works by exploiting an ancient set of biological defence mechanisms --- an evolved fear system, which we share with other animals. But humans are uniquely imaginative, and we use our evolved imagination to travel into virtual worlds that are full of danger.",
      "block_bbox": [
        66,
        577,
        1124,
        664
      ],
      "block_id": 9,
      "block_order": 10,
      "group_id": 9,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          66.0,
          577.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          577.0
        ],
        [
          1124.0,
          664.0
        ],
        [
          66.0,
          664.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "There are good reasons for watching a horror film. even if you're not a loyal horror fan. If you make it through the film in one piece, you'll probably experience a strong sense of mastery, a sense that you were able to make it through an appalling experience. Anyway, watching a horror film makes you better at handling your own fear, and who knows when that will become critically relevant?",
      "block_bbox": [
        67,
        670,
        1125,
        790
      ],
      "block_id": 10,
      "block_order": 11,
      "group_id": 10,
      "block_polygon_points": [
        [
          67.0,
          670.0
        ],
        [
          1125.0,
          670.0
        ],
        [
          1125.0,
          790.0
        ],
        [
          67.0,
          790.0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "46. The alien finds the audience in the movie theatre clearly in a state of\nA) total mindfulness          C) spiritual elevation\nB) extreme excitement        D) intense curiosity",
